CMP: \par
\par
If I forgot the accuracy of the odd quotation in the exam, would marks be taken off for using paraphrasing that part of the text instead of exactly precise quotations? \par
\par
AM: \par
\par
It is worth bearing in mind that referencing is just as useful as quoting in Section B of Paper 1 (e.g. I wouldn\rquote t bother to remember any quotations from Act 3, Scene 4 of The Duchess of Malfi \f1\endash  \ldblquote\'85Here the ceremony of the Cardinal\rquote s instalment, in the\f0\u8239?habit of a soldier\'85\rdblquote  \f1\endash  instead I would just refer to \ldblquote\'85Act 3, Scene 4, a scene in which every Protestant in Webster\rquote s audience\rquote s worst fears are realised \endash  we see the sword that lies beneath the Catholic clergyman\rquote s surplice\'85\rdblquote ).  \par
\par
It is better to be accurate if you can be, but more important is to remember to mark line ending when quoting poetry. \par
